<h2>About the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ef-themes</code></h2>

<p>The <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ef-themes</code> are a collection of light and dark themes for GNU
Emacs that provide colourful (“pretty”) yet legible options for users
who want something with a bit more flair than the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">modus-themes</code> (also
designed by me).</p>

<p>Starting with version <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">2.0.0</code>, the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ef-themes</code> are built on top of the
<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">modus-themes</code>. This means that all customisation options of the Modus
themes apply to the Ef themes. Same for all Modus commands that load a
theme. Enable <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ef-themes-take-over-modus-themes-mode</code> to set up this
arrangement (or enable <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">modus-themes-include-derivatives-mode</code> instead
to blend Ef and Modus into one collection).</p>

